 "about": "Whole-plate FDTD (otahub.num.patch_fdtd.pifa_ringdown) of planar inverted-F plates on air shorted by a strip at one corner. Each plate (tag) was run with a full-width short (ns = nw) and with corner strips ns cells wide; nh cells across the height h, nl along the plate from the shorted edge, nw across it. f is the resonance in cycles per cell-time, Q the total Q. A strip run's frequency is corrected by its plate's full-width run against the 0.2425-wavelength calibration (L + h = 0.2425 lambda): lambda = (1 + eps)/f with eps = f_full (nl + nh)/0.2425 - 1. Plates with W/L above 1.6 (tags ending s0.6 at W 0.2) excite another mode with the full-width short (eps 0.35-0.43) and are not used. convergence: one plate (h 0.05, W 0.15 wavelengths) at nh 4 and 6 for the grid error.",
